spec ri01-edge-create-vs-endpoint-delete: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# RI01. s1 DETACH DELETEs b; s2, whose snapshot predates s1's commit, creates a->b.
# In every order one of the two is refused: an edge create checks its destination's
# existence and adjacency (rmp #2444), and a node removal claims the node's adjacency, so
# an append committed after the remover's snapshot refuses the removal.
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s1d s1c s2e s2c
step s1d: MATCH (b:N {name:'b'}) DETACH DELETE b RETURN count(*) AS deleted
deleted
-------
1      
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2e: MATCH (a:N {name:'a'}), (b:N {name:'b'}) CREATE (a)-[:R {id:1}]->(b) RETURN count(*) AS created
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: cypher: transaction poisoned by a prior failed Exec statement — call Rollback
final final: MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name
name
----
"a" 
(1 row)
final edges: MATCH (x)-[r]->(y) RETURN x.name AS src, r.id AS id, y.name AS dst ORDER BY src, id, dst
src|id|dst
